"""Build a readable comparison and listening page from real saved observations."""
import json,html,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
source=ROOT/'reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.json'
data=json.loads(source.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def pct(value):return 'Unavailable' if value is None else f'{100*value:.2f}%'
lines=['# Prerecorded accent comparison against David','', 'Date: October 25, 2026. One hosted native file-audio run per synthetic voice. SDK '+data['sdk_version']+'.','', '## What changed','', 'Added six matched recordings: Windows SAPI David (US), Microsoft neural Guy (US control), Ryan (British), Prabhat (Indian), William (Australian), and Abeo (Nigerian). These are synthetic locale-labelled voice samples, not recordings of independent human speakers.','', 'Every voice reads the same neutral sentence. No patient records, verification credentials, financial context or personal data were sent to the external TTS service. The script tests a weekday, time-of-day phrase, two arbitrary digit sequences and a negative preference.','', '> '+data['rows'][0]['reference_text'],'', 'Pipeline: shared script -> selected TTS voice -> prerecorded PCM16 WAV -> common 16 kHz mono format -> 8 seconds leading / 3 seconds trailing silence -> native Guava Agent.test_audio -> caller-speech events -> independent scoring.','', 'The new probe is isolated from HarborCare healthcare workflows and does not replace the main agent or live phone listener. It measures file-audio transcription, not business workflow completion.','', '## Actual results','', '| Voice / locale | Raw WER | Numeral-normalized WER | Delta vs David (raw, pp) | Exact digit sequences | Negative cue observed |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|']
table=[];cards=[]
for row in data['rows']:
    count=sum(target in row.get('test_sequences_observed',[]) for target in ('1234','5678'))
    exact='2/2, correct order' if row.get('exact_test_sequences') else f'{count}/2; mismatch'
    negative='Yes' if row.get('negative_word_observed') else 'No / unavailable'
    delta=row.get('literal_wer_delta_vs_david_pp');delta='Unavailable' if delta is None else f'{delta:+.2f}'
    lines.append(f"| {row['label']} | {pct(row.get('literal_wer'))} | {pct(row.get('numeral_wer'))} | {delta} | {exact} | {negative} |")
    table.append('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(x))+'</td>' for x in [row['label'],pct(row.get('literal_wer')),pct(row.get('numeral_wer')),delta,exact,negative])+'</tr>')
    hyp=row.get('hypothesis') or 'No transcript available'
    lines+=[]
    cards.append(f'<article><h3>{html.escape(row["label"])}</h3><audio controls preload="none" src="assets/accents/{row["id"]}.wav"></audio><p><strong>Recognized:</strong> {html.escape(hyp)}</p><small>Voice: {html.escape(row["voice_id"])} · {row["speech_seconds"]} seconds speech · {html.escape(row["scoring_status"])}</small></article>')
lines+=['','Raw WER compares normalized words without converting spoken number words to digits. Numeral-normalized WER applies the same digit-word joining to reference and hypothesis. The two exact sequences must be 1234 and 5678 in order, with no extra digit sequence. The negative cue is a lexical observation, not proof of semantic consent handling.','','In this run, David, US Guy, British Ryan and Australian William matched after numeral normalization. Indian Prabhat returned the first sequence as "1 to 34" and omitted "The" before "first". Nigerian Abeo omitted the entire first-reference sentence from the captured transcript. Both retained 5678 and the negative cue. These are script-to-captured-transcript differences, not isolated proof of an accent-specific ASR defect: synthesis, endpointing and event capture have not been independently separated.','','## Transcripts','']
for row in data['rows']:lines+=['### '+row['label'],'','Recognized: '+str(row.get('hypothesis') or 'No transcript available'),'']
lines+=['## Interpretation and limits','','This is one identical script and one trial per voice; it cannot establish that any accent is generally easier or harder. A zero numeral-normalized score means the normalized reference matched in this sample, not general perfect recognition. Raw numeral-format differences are not necessarily lost information.','','David uses Windows SAPI; the others use Microsoft online neural synthesis, including MP3 decoding and linear resampling to 16 kHz. The US neural control helps show a possible engine effect but does not isolate accent from speaker, pace, timbre or codec. Default rates were retained and speech durations differ. No added noise, repeated trials, human-accent population, live microphone or carrier path was tested. Voice locale labels were not independently validated by a human listening panel.','','## Reproduce','', '1. Run scripts/setup-windows.ps1 for the pinned SDK/reporting environments.','2. Create baseline/audio-fixtures/.venv with uv and sync baseline/audio-fixtures/requirements.lock.txt into it.','3. Run scripts/build_accent_fixtures.py with that generator interpreter. David requires the installed Windows David SAPI voice; other voices use Microsoft online TTS via edge-tts 7.3.1.','4. With your Guava authentication available, run scripts/run_accent_comparison.py using baseline/sdk-0.47.0/.venv/Scripts/python.exe. This makes six hosted audio tests and may consume usage. Each has a 90-second process limit; errors/timeouts remain explicit.','5. Run scripts/build_accent_report.py with the SDK interpreter to rebuild the report/listening page.','','## Files and provenance','','- fixtures/audio/accents/manifest.json: exact voice IDs, shared reference, PCM format, padding, duration and SHA-256 for each file.','- tests/audio/accent_probe.py: native file-audio harness and utterance-event capture.','- tests/audio/accent_scoring.py: literal/numeric normalization and exact digit checks.','- scripts/run_accent_comparison.py: sequential one-trial execution with timestamped preserved raw logs/audio.','- dashboard/accent-comparison.html: scores, playback and recognized transcripts.','- reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.json: actual observations and provenance.','- Raw local evidence: evidence/accent-comparison/'+data['run_id']+'/ (ignored by Git).','','Run ID: `'+data['run_id']+'`. Locked source baseline commit: `'+data['source_commit']+'`; the newly added harness is a working-tree extension to that baseline. Input manifest SHA-256: `'+data['manifest_sha256']+'`.','','Voice generation package: [edge-tts project](https://github.com/rany2/edge-tts). Locale background: [Microsoft speech language support](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/speech-service/language-support). Generated fixture reuse remains subject to applicable provider terms; no human dataset license is claimed.']
report='\n'.join(lines)+'\n'
(ROOT/'reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.md').write_text(report,encoding='utf-8')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>AEGIS | Prerecorded accent comparison</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#edf2f3;color:#19343c;font:16px/1.6 system-ui}header{padding:32px 5vw;background:#163d44;color:white}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:24px}section,article{background:white;border:1px solid #dbe4e6;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin-bottom:18px}h1{margin:8px 0}h2{margin-top:0}a{color:#137269;font-weight:650}.scroll{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{padding:12px 8px;border-bottom:1px solid #dbe4e6;text-align:left}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}.cards article{margin:0}audio{max-width:100%;width:100%}small{color:#566d74}.note{background:#fff5df}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:700px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:12px}}</style></head><body><header><small style="color:#a3dbce">AEGIS CARE / OCTOBER 25, 2026</small><h1>Same script. Six prerecorded voices.</h1><p>David baseline · US neural control · British · Indian · Australian · Nigerian English</p></header><main><section><p><a href="lab.html">Improvement lab</a> · <a href="audio-comparison.html">Existing audio comparison</a> · <a href="../reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.md">Full methodology and change walkthrough</a></p><h2>One hosted test per voice</h2><p>These are synthetic locale-labelled samples, not a human-accent benchmark. Same text and padding, clean PCM16 mono 16 kHz input. No main-agent or live-phone changes.</p><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Voice / locale</th><th>Raw WER</th><th>Numeral-normalized WER</th><th>Delta vs David (pp)</th><th>Digit sequences</th><th>Negative cue</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(table)+'''</tbody></table></div><p>Raw WER retains number-format differences. Numeral-normalized WER compares “one two three four” with “1234” as equivalent. Exact digit checks still reject extra or wrong digits.</p></section><section class="note"><h2>What this comparison can tell us</h2><p>One sample per voice can reveal errors in this script; it cannot rank accents or establish general accuracy. Accent, speaker and synthesis engine are confounded. David is Windows SAPI; other samples are neural TTS. No human listening panel or repeated/noisy trials were run.</p></section><section><h2>Shared reference</h2><p>'''+html.escape(data['rows'][0]['reference_text'])+'''</p><p>Listen to each exact input below and compare it with the transcript Guava returned. Playback does not run another test.</p></section><div class="cards">'''+''.join(cards)+'''</div><section style="margin-top:18px"><h2>Reproducibility</h2><p>Six voices × one prerecorded clip × one hosted run. Hashes, voice IDs, duration, actual transcripts and metrics are retained. Process time is not ASR latency.</p><p>Run: <code>'''+data['run_id']+'''</code></p><p><a href="../reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.json">Machine-readable results</a> · <a href="../reports/test-results/accent-comparison-2026-10-25.md">Walkthrough and rerun instructions</a></p></section></main></body></html>'''
(ROOT/'dashboard/accent-comparison.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
print('Built accent comparison report and listening page')
